[% IF html %]<p>[% END -%]
It's been a while since i cleaned out the nginx logs,
now that my finals are out of the way [well, the hard
ones for me at least :]  But before I do that I prefer
to not have to worry about new logs coming in.  Stuff
like telling nginx where to write the access/error logs
and logrotate are going to create a mess if I don't
set them up right...
[%- IF html %]</p>[% ELSE %]
[% END -%]

[% IF html %]<p>[% END -%]
So I decided to schedule a DOWNTIME!  Basically, the
server will be down for real this time (there wouldn't
even be a maintenance page).  This affects [% IF html %]<em>all</em>[% ELSE %]*all*[% END %] sites
besides this status and the URL shortener (a.rdks.org),
which are the only sites hosted by Codeberg Pages.
Though I think no one would be [% IF html %]<em>seriously</em>[% ELSE %]*seriously*[% END %] affected by
this, so I won't give you too much time prepare.
[%- IF html %]</p>[% ELSE %]
[% END -%]

[% IF html %]<p>[% END -%]
Things I want to do besides exporting nginx logs include:
[%- IF html %]</p>[% ELSE %]
[% END -%]
[%- IF html %]<ol>[% ELSE %]
[% END -%]
  [% IF html %]<li>[% ELSE %] a) [% END %]set www.rapidcow.org as the canonical domain
[%- IF html %]</li>[% END %]
  [% IF html %]<li>[% ELSE %] b) [% END %]clean up my server files scattered over /home and
      /var/www/ (and update the nginx rules, obviously)
[%- IF html %]</li>[% END %]
  [% IF html %]<li>[% ELSE %] c) [% END %]and probably learn how to use logrotate so that
      I'm not looking at thousands of lines at once...
      also i want to see how i can do this more regularly
      and easily (and maybe even get GoAccess to work?)
[%- IF html %]</li>
</ol>[% ELSE %]
[% END %]

[% IF html %]<p>[% END -%]
The exact period of maintenance is... I'm not sure.
But the plan is that it would be back within 24 hours of
the publish date of this post (so Sat thru Sun, UTC 2 AM).
The HTTP(S) ports might get turned on and off during this
period (so don't be surprised if you see the sites still
running -- I might still be working!) If I need more time
than that, I'll let you know :)
[%- IF html %]</p>[% ELSE %]
